            "review_title": "Review at Le Jardin Restaurant",
            "review_text": "Jean Paul C\nParis, France54 contributions\n1\nIndustrial food\nNov 2016 • Friends\nI have stayed in hanoi 9 days to work and enjoy Vietnam International Fashion Week. After the runway show held at the Natonal Convention Center, Hotel Plaza was the closest to this venue distant form downtown Hanoi to come nd have a drink ofr food... But after the shows was very ofthe too late for a real dinner, Most times , the \"Le Jardin\" restaurant was closed. So after Fashion Week had finished I came here with a Vietnamese friend, as I was very much lookinfg forward to testing this restaurant which was always closed when we needed to eat. By the way, most restaurants in Vietnam close at 10:00 p.m.... So if you are looking for late dinner, street restaurants are often the only option. I believe that Vietnam should be thinking more of international \"jetlagged \"tourists who ight be nugry at 11;00 p.m; \nH_So , in this disposition, we went very early at this restaurant. It is big. the decor could be better... the white flowers i origami overlooking the various bufffets do not match very weel the materials and colours of beige /brown in the restaurant room. princes are Mid-range. The presnetation of food is pretentious... and not tasty enough in my opinion. For instance , I know we arrived early, but we ordered a tiramisu for desert. The presentation was nice with white chocolate strips curled up on top of the Italaina cake, fruit,- jelly etc;.. in a bu-ig protion. But when we tatsted the Toramisu... It had been frozen , had not had time to return to room temperature od -r slightly below... and it felt like having an icecube in your mouth... We could not eat it. Of course we mentionned it to the management who immediately siggested that the two protions we had ordered and started to eat would not be counted in our bill. This is nice. However, although the restaurant went to tell one of the chefs about it, the only thing we got was a galanec from this arther old EI-Uropean person? not one word of excuse or explanation for the desert which had ruined our dinner party which we had palnned to be nice and friendly.\nDommage 5 french expression meaning \"too bad\"... in a more sublte manner).\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten November 19, 2016",
